        {
          "id": "mha-9",
          "type": "text",
          "data": {
            "html": "<p>We never strip the top brood box in October. As goldenrod and wild ivy finish blooming along the hedgerows, our forty-eight Langstroth colonies have sealed enough dark, mineral-rich stores to carry them through February frosts.</p>",
